{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy ran on an untagged branch commit: add beta-only tag filters",
    "Explanation": [
      "The provided run (workflow_2.txt) finished SUCCESS for every job, so the pipeline itself is green. However, the behaviour is wrong: the trigger was a plain branch commit on `koans-09-tag-filters` with no tag, yet `deploy` still executed. By default CircleCI runs jobs on all branches and on NO tags, so the current config does the exact opposite of the requirement — it deploys on every branch commit and would never deploy on a tag push.",
      "",
      "The fix is to add a `filters` block in the *workflow* job declarations that ignores all branches and only allows tags matching the beta pattern, e.g.:",
      "",
      "```yaml",
      "filters:",
      "  branches:",
      "    ignore: /.*/",
      "  tags:",
      "    only: /^beta-.*/",
      "```",
      "",
      "Crucially, in CircleCI a job will not run for a tag unless every job it `requires` also has a tag filter. Since `deploy` requires `test`, which requires `build`, putting the filter only on `deploy` would mean `build` and `test` never run on the tag pipeline and therefore `deploy` would never be reached. The filter must therefore be applied to all jobs in the workflow (build, test and deploy), so the whole chain runs only on `beta-*` tags and is skipped for `alpha-*` tags and untagged branch commits — yielding a correct, green workflow when a tag like `beta-main-0.1.1` is pushed."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
