    "Title": "Persist app files to workspace",
    "Explanation": [
      "What happened: All three build jobs succeeded and wrote both app files (app/\u003cplatform\u003e/app.\u003cplatform\u003e) and meta files (meta/\u003cplatform\u003e/build.txt) into the job workspace filesystem. However, each build job persisted only meta/\u003cplatform\u003e to the workspace. The deploy job attached the workspace and therefore only received the persisted meta files (meta/linux/build.txt, meta/mac/build.txt, meta/windows/build.txt). The deploy job's verification step expected app/linux/app.linux, app/windows/app.windows, and app/mac/app.mac to exist, but they were never persisted, so the tests failed and deploy exited with status 1. Evidence: job_6.log shows only meta/* files in the workspace listing and the three test -f checks failed. Fix: persist the generated app files (app/\u003cplatform\u003e) from each build into the workspace so the final deploy job receives them and can upload them as artifacts. Concretely, change each build-\u003cplatform\u003e.persist_to_workspace.paths to include the app/\u003cplatform\u003e directory (or persist the entire app directory), for example:",
      "- persist_to_workspace:",
      "    root: .",
      "    paths:",
      "      - app/linux",
      "      - meta/linux",
      "(and similarly for windows and mac). Alternatively persist root: . with paths: [app, meta] if acceptable. The deploy job’s store_artifacts step can then successfully find and upload app/*.",
      "",
      "Why the other options are not chosen: store_artifacts_on_builds_only would upload artifacts from builds instead of using workspace—this changes the intended flow of collecting all apps in deploy. fix_one_platform_only, change_attach_only, and remove_verify_only do not address the root cause (the app files were never persisted to the workspace)."
